204: ## System Setup Guide
205: 
206: Follow these steps to set up and run the codebase on **Windows**, **macOS**, or **Linux**.
207: 
208: ### 1. Prerequisites
209: - **Python 3.8+** (Python 3.10+ recommended)
210: - **Git**
211: - *(Optional)* **CUDA-capable GPU** with drivers installed if running local neural models (TrOCR/PyTorch) with hardware acceleration.
212: 
213: Verify Python version:
214: ```bash
215: python --version
216: # or
217: python3 --version
218: ```
219: 
220: ### 2. Clone & Navigate
221: Clone the repository (or extract the source code) and navigate into the root directory:
222: ```bash
223: git clone <repository_url>
224: cd OCR_codes
225: ```
226: 
227: ### 3. Set Up Virtual Environment
228: 
229: Create and activate an isolated Python virtual environment:
230: 
231: - **Windows (PowerShell):**
232:   ```powershell
233:   python -m venv venv
234:   .\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
235:   ```
236: 
237: - **Windows (Command Prompt):**
238:   ```cmd
239:   python -m venv venv
240:   venv\Scripts\activate.bat
241:   ```
242: 
243: - **macOS / Linux (Bash or Zsh):**
244:   ```bash
245:   python3 -m venv venv
246:   source venv/bin/activate
247:   ```
248: 
249: ### 4. Install Dependencies
250: 
251: Upgrade `pip` and install all required packages:
252: ```bash
253: pip install --upgrade pip
254: pip install -r requirements.txt
255: ```
256: 
257: > **Note on PyTorch (GPU Acceleration):**  
258: > `requirements.txt` installs standard CPU PyTorch packages by default. To enable GPU acceleration with CUDA on Windows/Linux, install CUDA PyTorch binaries from the [official PyTorch website](https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/):
259: > ```bash
260: > pip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121
261: > ```
262: 
263: ### 5. Environment Configuration
264: 
265: Create or update the `.env` file in the root project directory with your credentials:
266: 
267: ```env
268: MISTRAL_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
269: ```
270: 
271: ### 6. OCR Backend Prerequisites (LM Studio / TrOCR)
272: 
273: - **LM Studio (Default Backend):**
274:   1. Download and open [LM Studio](https://lmstudio.ai/).
275:   2. Load a Vision LLM model (e.g., Qwen2-VL, Llama-3-Vision).
276:   3. Start the **Local Inference Server** inside LM Studio (default URL: `http://localhost:1234`).
277: - **TrOCR Backend:**
278:   1. Standard PyTorch environment; required models will automatically download from HuggingFace on first run.
279: 
